# The files Docker leaves out when it sends the repository to a build as its context. Today no
# image builds from the repository's root: db/Dockerfile builds from db/ alone. This file guards
# any later image that does, so the build stays small and no secret enters an image.

# Build output: each image builds its own, so a copy from this machine only slows the build.
**/bin/
**/obj/
# Git's history: no image needs it, and it grows with every commit.
.git/
# This machine's passwords: anything in a build's context can end up in an image layer.
.env
# Installed packages: an image installs its own, for its own system, and these are large.
**/node_modules/
# Tests, documents and raw places: the running service needs none of them.
tests/
docs/
data/
